# Revert to Previous User Message

## Context

Users currently have no way to undo a back-and-forth chunk of a session — once the agent runs tool calls and edits files, the only escape is to abandon the task. We want a per-user-message **Revert** button that:

- Truncates the chat visually back to that message (the message itself returns to the composer as a draft).
- Restores the working tree (and index/HEAD) to the git checkpoint that was captured just before that message was sent.
- Forks the agent's conversation at that point so subsequent turns continue from the correct prefix.

Constraints decided up front:

- **Agent-agnostic surface, Claude-only behaviour.** The capability is exposed via `agentCapabilities._meta.posthog.revert` and only the Claude adapter implements it. Codex/cloud is out of scope.
- **No cloud.** Revert is disabled when the active session is a cloud run (`session.isCloud`).
- We do **not** start a new Claude session id, and we do **not** fork. The Claude `sessionId` and its on-disk transcript are reused. But because `resumeSessionAt` is a constructor option to the SDK's `query({ prompt, options })`, we **must respawn the agent's `Query` instance** (and the underlying `claude-code` child process) with the new `Options`. This is exactly what the existing `refreshSession()` path already does for MCP option changes — we extend it to honor a `resumeSessionAt` from the refresh `_meta`. The SDK's slice-on-resume behavior is what truncates the model's view at `index + 1` of the matching `uuid` (see `loadInitialMessages` in claude-agent-sdk).
- Mid-turn revert is **disabled**: the button is gated on `!isPromptPending`.

## Design summary

We introduce three small, decoupled pieces:

1. **Two UUIDs per user message.** An ACP-level UUID (ours, durable, used for revert markers and log filtering) and the Claude SDK UUID (theirs, used by `resumeSessionAt`). Both ride on `_meta.posthog` of session updates.
2. **A per-user-message git checkpoint.** Captured by the main-process agent service immediately before forwarding the prompt to the agent, persisted as the existing `_posthog/git_checkpoint` notification with a new `userMessageId` field.
3. **A revert marker** (`_posthog/revert`) appended to the session log. The renderer's conversation builder honors markers by truncating items past the targeted ACP UUID. The Claude adapter respawns its `Query` (same `sessionId`, fresh `claude-code` child process) with `resume + resumeSessionAt` so the next prompt continues from the right point.

This avoids new tables and new storage shapes — everything piggybacks on the existing log + git checkpoint primitives.

## File-by-file changes

### 1. ACP extension surface — `packages/agent/src/acp-extensions.ts`

Add a marker:

```ts
REVERT: "_posthog/revert",
```

Document the payload shape in a sibling `revert.ts`:

```ts
// packages/agent/src/revert.ts
export interface RevertMarker {
  /** ACP UUID of the user message we reverted to. */
  acpMessageId: string;
  /** Claude SDK uuid of the assistant message that immediately precedes the user message. Used as resumeSessionAt. */
  claudeSdkUuidBeforeRevert: string | null;
  /** Optional checkpoint id this revert restored to (for diagnostics). */
  checkpointId?: string;
  /** ISO timestamp. */
  timestamp: string;
}
```

### 2. UUID propagation in the Claude adapter

**`packages/agent/src/adapters/claude/claude-agent.ts`** (`broadcastUserMessage`, ~line 1583):

- Generate `acpMessageId = uuidv7()` once per `prompt()`.
- Attach to every chunk: `update._meta = { posthog: { acpMessageId } }`.
- Return the id from `broadcastUserMessage` so `prompt()` can include it on later notifications (turn_complete, etc.) if desired.

**`packages/agent/src/adapters/claude/conversion/sdk-to-acp.ts`** (`handleUserAssistantMessage`):

- For SDK assistant messages, when emitting `agent_message_chunk` / `agent_message`, include the SDK `uuid` on `update._meta = { posthog: { sdkUuid: msg.uuid } }`. This is the value we'll later pass to `resumeSessionAt`.
- For SDK result messages in `handleResultMessage`, also stamp `_meta.posthog.sdkUuid` (the SDK result message also has a uuid we can use as a fallback).

Do **not** modify the Codex adapter — Codex won't expose `revert: true`, so its messages don't need these fields. Keeping it Claude-only avoids leaking SDK-specific concepts into Codex.

### 3. Capability advertisement — `packages/agent/src/adapters/claude/claude-agent.ts` (`initialize`)

Extend the `_meta.posthog` block (around lines 196–199):

```ts
_meta: {
  posthog: { resumeSession: true, revert: true },
  claudeCode: { promptQueueing: true },
},
```

Codex's `initialize` keeps `posthog: { resumeSession: true }` only.

### 4. `resumeSessionAt` plumbing

**`packages/agent/src/adapters/claude/session/options.ts`** (`BuildOptionsParams`, `buildSessionOptions`):

- Add `resumeSessionAt?: string` to `BuildOptionsParams`.
- In `buildSessionOptions`, when `params.isResume && params.resumeSessionAt`, set `options.resumeSessionAt = params.resumeSessionAt`.

**`packages/agent/src/adapters/claude/claude-agent.ts`** (`createSession`, `unstable_resumeSession`):

- Thread `resumeSessionAt` through `creationOpts` and pass to `buildSessionOptions`.
- Accept it on the request via `_meta.posthog.resumeSessionAt` so the main process can ask for it without inventing a new ACP method.

### 5. New main-process service: `RevertService`

**`apps/code/src/main/services/revert/service.ts`** (new):

Owns the orchestration. Inputs come over tRPC; outputs are tRPC notifications + log appends.

```ts
@injectable()
export class RevertService {
  async revertToMessage(input: { taskRunId: string; acpMessageId: string }) {
    // 1. Guard: refuse if a turn is in flight (caller also gates the UI).
    // 2. Read the session log from packages/agent SessionLogWriter / cache.
    // 3. Resolve targets:
    //    - The user_message_chunk entry whose _meta.posthog.acpMessageId === acpMessageId.
    //    - The latest agent_message_chunk OR result entry BEFORE that user message; take its _meta.posthog.sdkUuid.
    //    - The latest _posthog/git_checkpoint whose params.userMessageId === acpMessageId.
    // 4. RevertCheckpointSaga.run(checkpointState) via packages/git.
    // 5. Append revert marker via SessionLogWriter (method = "_posthog/revert").
    // 6. Respawn the Query (and its claude-code child process) with the same
    //    sessionId but new Options carrying resumeSessionAt = sdkUuidBeforeRevert.
    //    Send `_posthog/refresh_session` with _meta.posthog.resumeSessionAt. The
    //    Claude adapter's existing refreshSession() path already tears down and
    //    recreates Query for MCP option changes; extend its option-build to honor
    //    resumeSessionAt the same way createSession does. No new sessionId, no
    //    forkSession — just a fresh Query against the same transcript with a
    //    truncated view.
    // 7. Emit a `_posthog/revert` notification on the session so the renderer
    //    invalidates and re-derives its conversation items.
  }
}
```

Capture site for new checkpoints (also lives in `RevertService` to keep concerns together, or in the existing agent service if there's already a pre-prompt hook):

**`apps/code/src/main/services/agent/service.ts`** — wherever the renderer's `agent.prompt` mutation forwards into the in-process ACP connection. Just before forwarding:

- Call `CaptureCheckpointSaga` from `packages/git/src/sagas/checkpoint.ts` with `checkpointId = ` `posthog-code-msg-${acpMessageId}` (acpMessageId generated client-side and threaded into the prompt request _meta — see §6).
- Append a `_posthog/git_checkpoint` notification via the existing log writer with `params.userMessageId = acpMessageId` (extend `GitCheckpointEvent` type in `packages/agent/src/types.ts`).
- This reuses `findLatestGitCheckpoint` style scanning in `ResumeSaga`; we add a `findCheckpointForUserMessage(entries, acpMessageId)` sibling helper that filters by `userMessageId`.

Cloud runs skip checkpoint capture (`session.isCloud` short-circuits).

### 6. Generating the ACP UUID up front

Today `broadcastUserMessage` mints the UUID inside the Claude adapter, but the main process needs the same UUID to label the checkpoint *before* the prompt is forwarded. Move the generation up:

- Renderer composer generates `acpMessageId = uuidv7()` when the user submits.
- Pass it as `_meta.posthog.acpMessageId` on the `agent.prompt` tRPC mutation.
- Main-process agent service uses it for the checkpoint label.
- Claude adapter's `broadcastUserMessage` reads it from `params._meta.posthog.acpMessageId` (falling back to `uuidv7()` if absent, for backward compat) instead of minting its own.

This keeps the ID single-sourced.

### 7. tRPC

**`apps/code/src/main/trpc/routers/`** — add a `revert.ts` router with a `revertToMessage` mutation. Wire it into the root router. Input validated with Zod: `{ taskRunId: string, acpMessageId: string }`.

### 8. Renderer

**Filtering on the conversation builder** — `apps/code/src/renderer/features/sessions/components/buildConversationItems.ts`:

- Walk events once, indexing each user message by `_meta.posthog.acpMessageId`.
- When a `_posthog/revert` notification is encountered, drop every conversation item whose backing event sits **after** the indexed user message (and drop the user message itself; per the spec it returns to the composer as a draft).
- Subsequent events after the marker append normally; if a *later* revert marker appears, repeat.

**User message UI** — `apps/code/src/renderer/features/sessions/components/session-update/UserMessage.tsx`:

- Accept new props: `acpMessageId?: string`, `canRevert?: boolean`, `onRevert?: () => void`.
- Add an `IconButton` (e.g. `ArrowCounterClockwise`) next to the existing copy button inside the existing `group/msg` hover container (lines 158–174). Render only when `canRevert && onRevert`.

**Modal + mutation host** — `apps/code/src/renderer/features/sessions/components/ConversationView.tsx`:

- Local state: `const [revertTarget, setRevertTarget] = useState<{ id: string; content: string } | null>(null)`.
- Pass `acpMessageId={item.id}`, `canRevert={canRevertHere}`, `onRevert={() => setRevertTarget({ id: item.id, content: item.content })}` to each `<UserMessage>` (line 175).
- `canRevertHere = adapter === "claude" && !session?.isCloud && !isPromptPending && capabilities.revert === true`.
- On confirm: call `trpcClient.revert.revertToMessage.mutate({ taskRunId, acpMessageId })`; on success, push `revertTarget.content` into the composer draft (existing store action) and `toast.success("Reverted")`; on error, `toast.error(...)`.
- The `AlertDialog` mirrors `McpServersSettings` (lines 289–338) — title `Revert to this point?`, description per spec, actions `Cancel | Reset` (red `solid`).

**Capability hook** — extend whichever store/hook surfaces `agentCapabilities` so the renderer can read `_meta.posthog.revert` per session. The session metadata path that already feeds `useAdapterForTask` is the natural home.

### 9. Conversation item id ↔ ACP UUID

`buildConversationItems` already mints local incrementing ids for `ConversationItem.id`. We need the **ACP UUID** to drive revert. Add `acpMessageId` to the `user_message` variant of `ConversationItem`, populated from `update._meta.posthog.acpMessageId`. The local `id` stays as today.

